

- contains

  :: identity orientation::

 + may contain        (c)  - may make up part of    (cb)
 + contains           (contain)   - belongs to          (belong)
 + includes           (incl)      - is included in      (is-incl)
 + contains fragment  (has frag)  - is a fragment in    (is-frag)
 + has message body   (message body) - is the body of message (isbodmsg)

 + may be triggered by (>?) - may violate (<?)
 